{
  "$comment": "First-party plugin registry (AGL-417). THE single place that maps plugin ids to packages, register entry points, and API path prefixes. `tools/scripts/generate-plugin-manifests.mjs` turns this into the per-app generated loader manifests — the only files allowed to reference @aglyn/plugins-* outside libs/plugins. Ids must match FIRST_PARTY_PLUGINS in libs/aglyn plugin-manager/enabled-plugins.ts. register keys: site = canvas/site components (client barrel), console = ConsoleExtension (client barrel), tenantApi/consoleApi = API handlers (/server entry), declarations = the light registrations core reads before any surface loads (`/declarations`, both apps, client and server), serverDeclarations = the same for the server alone (`/declarations.server`, platform-event subscriptions), consoleServerDeclarations = the same for the CONSOLE's server alone (`/declarations.console-server`, never loaded or bundled by the tenant runtime: for registrations that open what only the console holds), subprocessors = the third-party recipients the plugin's code sends data to, and its other hosts and its uses of hosts declared elsewhere (`/subprocessors`, called by the generator rather than at runtime, and written into the console's subprocessors manifest as data for the subprocessor inventory). activityMutationPaths = the plugin's modules that create, transfer or destroy a durable customer object, which `tools/scripts/check-activity-coverage.mjs` holds to logging an activity entry like the platform's own. `alwaysOn` here is the LOADER's meaning — the bundle activates whatever ids `ensure()` is given, so it defeats the per-page narrowing in required-site-plugins.ts and belongs only to `mui`, which the canvas cannot render without. A plugin that merely may not be switched OFF says so with `alwaysOn` in FIRST_PARTY_PLUGINS instead.",
  "plugins": [
    {
      "id": "mui",
      "package": "@aglyn/plugins-mui",
      "alwaysOn": true,
      "register": {
        "site": "registerMuiPlugin"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "forms",
      "package": "@aglyn/plugins-forms",
      "register": {
        "site": "registerFormsPlugin",
        "console": "registerFormsConsole"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bookings",
      "package": "@aglyn/plugins-bookings",
